---@alias aws.networkmanager.NatRuleList aws.networkmanager.NatRule[]

---@alias aws.networkmanager.NatRuleNumber number

---Describes a NAT rule to configure on an attachment. Source addresses in the source CIDR block of traffic from the attachment are translated to the same host addresses in the NAT CIDR block. Traffic to an address in the NAT CIDR block is translated back to the matching address in the source CIDR block.
---@class aws.networkmanager.NatRuleRequest
---@field RuleNumber aws.networkmanager.NatRuleNumber The rule number, from 1 to 32766. Each rule number must be unique for the attachment.
---@field MatchSourceCidr aws.networkmanager.IPAddress The IPv4 CIDR block to match against the source address of traffic from the attachment. The CIDR block can't overlap with the multicast range (224.0.0.0/4).
---@field NatCidr aws.networkmanager.IPAddress The IPv4 CIDR block to translate matching source addresses to. The prefix length must be the same as the prefix length of MatchSourceCidr. The CIDR block must be within a private (RFC 1918) or shared address space (RFC 6598) range. The CIDR blocks of the NAT rules of an attachment can't overlap with each other.

---@alias aws.networkmanager.NatRuleRequestList aws.networkmanager.NatRuleRequest[]

---@alias aws.networkmanager.NatRuleState "CREATING"|"MODIFYING"|"DELETING"|"ACTIVATED"|"ACTIVATING"|"DEACTIVATED"|"DEACTIVATING"|"FAILED"|"PENDING_ATTACHMENT_ACCEPTANCE"

