---@class aws.networkmanager.UpdateAttachmentNatConfigurationRequest
---@field AttachmentId aws.networkmanager.AttachmentId The ID of the attachment to update the NAT configuration for.
---@field NatGatewaySupport? aws.networkmanager.NatGatewaySupportValue|string Specifies whether to enable or disable NAT gateway support on the attachment. When you disable NAT gateway support, the attachment keeps its NAT rules but doesn't apply them. To enable NAT gateway support, the attachment must have at least one NAT rule, either specified in this request or already configured on the attachment. If you omit this parameter, NAT gateway support is unchanged.
---@field NatSystemRouteSupport? aws.networkmanager.BoxedBoolean Specifies whether the core network installs system routes for the NAT CIDR blocks of the attachment's NAT rules. System routes have a route type of SYSTEM. NAT is applied to traffic whether or not this option is enabled. If you omit this parameter, the current value is unchanged.
---@field NatGatewayRules? aws.networkmanager.NatRuleRequestList The complete set of NAT rules for the attachment, up to 50 rules. The rules that you specify replace the existing rules of the attachment, matched by rule number. Existing rules that aren't included in the request are deleted. To delete all NAT rules, specify an empty list. You can delete all NAT rules only when NAT gateway support is disabled, or when you disable it in the same request. If you om...
---@field ClientToken? aws.networkmanager.ClientToken The client token associated with the request.

---@class aws.networkmanager.UpdateAttachmentNatConfigurationResponse
---@field AttachmentId? aws.networkmanager.AttachmentId The ID of the attachment.
---@field NatGatewaySupport? aws.networkmanager.NatGatewaySupportState The state of NAT gateway support on the attachment. The transitional states ENABLING and DISABLING change to ENABLED or DISABLED after the update is applied. The state is PENDING_ATTACHMENT_ACCEPTANCE when NAT gateway support is enabled on an attachment that is pending acceptance.
---@field NatSystemRouteSupport? aws.networkmanager.BoxedBoolean Indicates whether the core network installs system routes for the NAT CIDR blocks of the attachment's NAT rules.
---@field NatGatewayRules? aws.networkmanager.NatRuleList The NAT rules of the attachment, including rules that are being deleted.

